{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-264870",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to each component of $w.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}(2{w}_{1}{x}_{1}-5{w}_{2}{x}_{2})=2{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}(2{w}_{1}{x}_{1}-5{w}_{2}{x}_{2})=-5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, with $x={[\\begin{aligned}-2,\\,8\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -40\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
